  "text": "[[845.13]] <b>178.  Non inelegans specimen demonstrandi in abstractis [Februar bis April 1687 (?)]</b>\n [[845.14]] <tab/>[Februar bis April 1687 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[846.11]] <k>Def.</k> 1. <b>Eadem</b> sunt quorum unum potest substitui alteri salva veritate. Si sint <i>A</i> et\n[[846.12]] <i>B</i> et <i>A</i> ingrediatur aliquam propositionem veram, et ibi in aliquo loco ipsius <i>A</i> pro ipso\n[[846.13]] substituendo <i>B</i>, fiat nova propositio, eaque itidem vera idque semper succedat in quacunque\n[[846.14]] tali propositione; <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> dicuntur esse <b>Eadem</b>, et contra, si Eadem sint <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>,\n[[846.15]] procedet substitutio quam dixi. Eadem etiam vocantur <b>coincidentia.</b> Aliquando tamen\n[[846.16]] <i>A</i> quidem et <i>A</i> vocantur <b>idem</b>; <i>A</i> vero et <i>B</i> si sint eadem vocantur <b>coincidentia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[846.17]] <k>Def.</k> 2. <b>Diversa</b> sunt quae sunt non eadem, seu in quibus substitutio aliquando non\n[[846.18]] succedit. </p>\n<p> [[846.19]] <k>Corollarium.</k> Unde etiam, quae non sunt diversa sunt eadem. </p>\n<p> [[846.20]] <k>Charact.</k> 1. <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> significat <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> esse <b>eadem</b> vel <b>coincidentia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[846.21]] <k>Charact.</k> 2. <i>A non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i>, vel <i>B non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i>, significat <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> esse <b>diversa.</b> </p>\n<p> [[846.22]] <k>Def.</k> 3. Si plura simul sumta coincidant uni; plurium quodlibet dicitur <b>inesse</b> vel\n[[846.23]] <b>contineri</b> in uno isto, ipsum autem Unum dicitur <b>continens.</b> Et contra, si quid insit\n[[846.24]] alteri, erit inter plura simul coincidentia illi alteri. Ut si <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> simul sumta coincidant ipsi\n[[846.25]] <i>L</i>; <i>A</i>, ut et <i>B</i> dicetur <b>inexistens</b> vel <b>contentum</b>; at <i>L</i> dicetur <b>continens.</b> Fieri\n[[846.26]] tamen potest, ut continens et contentum coincidant, ut si sit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i>, et coincidant <i>A</i> et\n[[846.27]] <i>L</i>, tunc enim <i>B</i> nihil aliud continebit quam <i>A</i>, sed si non significet <i>A</i>, significabit <i>Nihil</i>. </p>\n<p> [[846.28]] <k>Scholium.</k> Non omne inexistens est pars, nec omne continens est totum, ex. gr.\n[[846.29]] quadratum inscriptum, et diameter circulo inest; et quadratum quidem est pars circuli,\n[[847.1]] diameter vero non est pars ejus. Addendum est ergo aliquid ad notionem totius et partis\n[[847.2]] accurate explicandam, quod non est hujus loci. Et vero non insunt tantum, sed et detrahi\n[[847.3]] possunt ea quae partes non sunt, ex. gr. centrum ex circulo ita ut in residuo sint omnia\n[[847.4]] puncta praeter centrum; id enim residuum erit locus omnium punctorum intra circulum,\n[[847.5]] quorum distantia a circumferentia est minor radio, cujus loci differentia a circulo est\n[[847.6]] punctum, nempe centrum. Ita locus omnium punctorum quae moventur, sphaera duobus\n[[847.7]] ejus punctis diametro distantibus, immotis, mota, fit si a sphaera detrahas axem seu\n[[847.8]] diametrum per duo puncta immota transeuntem. </p>\n<p> [[847.9]] Iisdem positis, <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> simul sumta dicuntur <b>constituentia</b>, <i>L</i> autem <b>constitutum.</b> </p>\n<p> [[847.11]] <k>Charact.</k> 3. <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i> significat <i>A</i> <b>inesse</b> ipsi <i>L</i>, vel <b>contineri</b> a [<i>L</i>]. </p>\n<p> [[847.12]] <k>Scholium.</k> Etsi <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> habeant\n[[847.13]] aliquid commune, ita ut ambo simul\n[[847.14]] sint majora ipso <i>L</i>; nihilo minus locum\n[[847.15]] habebunt, quae hoc loco diximus aut\n[[847.16]] dicemus. Exemplo rem declarare utile\n[[847.17]] erit: <i>L</i> significet rectam <i>RX</i>, et <i>A</i> partem\n[[847.18]] ejus, rectam scilicet <i>RS</i>, et <i>B</i> aliam\n[[847.19]] ejus partem, rectam scilicet <i>XY</i>. Ponatur\n[[847.20]] quaelibet harum partium <i>RS</i>, vel <i>XY</i>\n[[847.21]] major esse dimidio totius <i>RX</i>; utique\n[[847.22]] non potest dici <i>A</i> + <i>B aequ. L</i> seu [<i>RS</i>]\n[[847.23]] + <i>XY aequ. RX.</i> Nam revera quia <i>YS</i> est\n[[847.24]] pars communis ipsarum <i>RS</i> et <i>XY</i>, erit\n[[847.25]] <i>RS</i> + <i>XY aequ. RX</i> + <i>SY</i>, et tamen vere\n[[847.26]] dici potest rectas <i>RS</i> et <i>XY</i> simul, coincidere rectae <i>RX.</i> </p>\n<p> [[847.27]] <k>Def.</k> 4. Si aliquid <i>M</i> insit ipsi <i>A</i> itemque insit ipsi <i>B</i>, id dicetur ipsis commune, ipsa\n[[847.28]] autem dicentur <b>communicantia.</b> Si vero nihil commune habeant, ut <i>A</i> et <i>N</i> (verbi\n[[847.29]] gratia rectae <i>RS</i> et <i>XS</i>) dicentur <b>incommunicantia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[848.1]] <k>Def.</k> 5. Si ipsi <i>L</i> insit <i>A</i>, et efficiatur aliud <i>N</i>, in quo omnia manent, quae sunt in <i>L</i>,\n[[848.2]] exceptis iis quae etiam sunt in <i>A</i>, quorum nihil manere debet in N, dicetur <i>A</i> <b>detrahi</b> vel\n[[848.3]] removeri ab <i>L</i>, at <i>N</i> dicetur <b>Residuum.</b> </p>\n<p> [[848.4]] <k>Charact.</k> 4. Si sit <i>L ─ A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i>, signi[fi]catur <i>L</i> esse continens, a quo si <b>detrahas</b> <i>A</i>\n[[848.5]] <b>residuum</b> sit <i>N.</i> </p>\n<p> [[848.6]] <k>Def.</k> 6. Si unum aliquod pluribus simul positis aut remotis coincidere ponatur, plura\n[[848.7]] illa dicuntur <b>constituentia</b>, unum autem <b>constitutum.</b> </p>\n<p> [[848.8]] <k>Scholium.</k> Hinc omnia quidem inexistentia sunt constituentia, sed non contra, ut\n[[848.9]] <i>L ─ A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i>, utique non inest <i>L</i> in [<i>N</i>]. </p>\n<p> [[848.10]] <k>Def.</k> 7. Constitutio (hoc est positio aut detractio) vel tacita vel expressa est.\n[[848.11]] Expressa ipsius [<i>M</i>] patet ut <i>M</i> vel <i>─M</i>, tacita ipsius <i>M</i>, ut <i>A</i> vel <i>─A</i> cui inest <i>M.</i> </p>\n<p> [[848.12]] <k>Def.</k> 8. <b>Compensatio</b> est, cum idem ponitur et detrahitur in eodem, expressa cum\n[[848.13]] expresse. <b>Destructio</b> est cum quid ob compensationem abjicitur, ut non amplius\n[[848.14]] exprimatur, ut pro <i>M ─ M</i> ponendo <i>Nihil</i>. </p>\n<p> [[848.15]] <k>Axioma</k> 1. Si idem secum ipso sumatur, nihil constituitur novum, seu <i>A</i> + <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i>. </p>\n<p> [[848.16]] <k>Scholium.</k> Equidem in numeris 2 + 2 facit [4], seu bini nummi binis additi faciunt\n[[848.17]] quatuor nummos, sed tunc bini additi sunt alii a prioribus; si iidem essent, nihil novi\n[[848.18]] prodiret, et perinde esset ac si joco, ex tribus ovis facere vellemus sex, numerando\n[[848.19]] primum 3 ova, deinde uno sublato residua 2, ac denique uno rursus sublato residuum 1. </p>\n<p> [[848.20]] <k>Axioma</k> 2. Si idem ponitur et detrahitur, quicquid inde in alio constituitur, coincidit\n[[848.21]] <i>Nihilo</i>. Seu <i>A</i> (quotiescunque in aliqua re constituenda ponitur) ─ <i>A</i> (quotiescunque ex\n[[848.22]] eadem detrahitur) ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i> </p>\n<p> [[848.23]] <k>Scholium.</k> Unde <i>A ─ A</i> vel ^#6+<i>A</i> + <i>A^#6- ─ A</i> vel <i>A ─ ^#6+A</i> + <i>A^#6-</i> etc. ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i> Nam per Ax. 1 res\n[[848.24]] semper redit ad <i>A ─ A.</i> </p>\n<p> [[848.25]] <k>Postulatum</k> 1. Plura quaecunque simul sumi possunt ad unum constituendum, ut si\n[[848.26]] sint <i>A</i>, et <i>B</i>, potest inde fieri <i>A</i> + <i>B</i>, quod appellari potest <i>L.</i> </p>\n<p> [[849.1]] <k>Postulatum</k> 2. Detrahere aliquid <i>A</i> ab eo cui inest nempe ab <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> seu <i>L</i>, si reliqua\n[[849.2]] dentur, ut <i>B</i>, quae cum ipso <i>A</i> constituunt continens <i>L</i>, seu iisdem positis invenire\n[[849.3]] Residuum <i>L ─ A.</i> </p>\n<p> [[849.4]] <k>Scholium.</k> Ope hujus postulati postea modum dabimus inveniendi differentiam\n[[849.5]] inter duo quorum unum <i>A</i> alteri <i>L</i> inest, licet reliqua quae cum illo hoc constituunt, non\n[[849.6]] dentur; seu modum inveniendi <i>L ─ A</i>, seu <i>A</i> + <i>B ─ A</i>, licet solum dentur <i>L</i> et <i>A</i>, non vero\n[[849.7]] <i>B.</i>\n [[849.8]] <k>Theorema I</k> </p>\n<p> [[849.9]] <b>Quae sunt eadem uni tertio, eadem sunt inter se.</b> </p>\n<p> [[849.10]] Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> erit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Nam si in propositione <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> (vera, ex hypothesi)\n[[849.11]] substituatur <i>C</i> in locum <i>B</i> (quod facere licet per def. 1, quia <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i>, ex hyp.) fiet <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i>\n[[849.12]] Q. E. Dem.\n [[849.13]] <k>Theorema II</k> </p>\n<p> [[849.14]] <b>Si duorum quae sunt eadem inter se, unum diversum sit a tertio,\n[[849.15]] etiam alterum ab eo erit diversum.</i> </p>\n<p> [[849.16]] Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> et <i>B non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> erit <i>A non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Nam si in propositione <i>B non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> (vera, ex\n[[849.17]] hyp.) substituatur <i>A</i> in locum <i>B</i> (quod facere licet per def. 1, quia <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> ex hyp.) fiet <i>A\n[[849.18]] non</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i>. Q. E. Dem.\n [[849.19]] <k>Theorema III</k> <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: Hic inseri posset Theorema tale: <b>Quod inest uni coincidentium, etiam alteri inest.</b> Si <i>A</i> est in [<i>B</i>] et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> etiam <i>A</i> est in <i>C</i>. Nempe in prop. <i>A est in B</i> (vera ex hyp.) substituendo <i>C</i> in locum ipsius <i>B</i>.</Fn> </p>\n<p> [[850.1]] <b>Si eidem addantur coincidentia, fiunt coincidentia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[850.2]] Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> erit <i>A</i> + <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> + <i>C</i>. Nam si in propositione <i>A</i> + <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>C</i> (quae est vera\n[[850.3]] per se) pro <i>A</i> semel substituas <i>B</i> (quod facere licet per def. 1, quia <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i>) fiet <i>A</i> + <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character>\n[[850.4]] <i>B</i> + <i>C.</i> Q. E. Dem.\n [[850.5]] <k>Corollarium</k> </p>\n<p> [[850.6]] <b>Si coincidentibus addantur coincidentia, fiunt coincidentia</b>. </p>\n<p> [[850.7]] Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> et <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i> erit <i>A</i> + <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> + <i>M</i>. Nam (per praesens theorema) quia <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i>\n[[850.8]] erit <i>A</i> + <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>M</i> et in hac assertione pro <i>A</i> semel ponendo <i>B</i> (quia <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> ex hyp.) fiet <i>A</i>\n[[850.9]] + <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> + <i>M</i>. Q. E. Dem.\n [[850.10]] <k>Theorema IV</k> </p>\n<p> [[850.11]] <b>Contentum contenti est contentum continentis.</b> </p>\n<p> [[850.12]] Seu si id cui aliud inest, insit tertio, id quod ei inest eidem tertio inerit, vel si <i>A</i> est in\n[[850.13]] <i>B</i> et <i>B</i> est in <i>C</i>, etiam <i>A</i> erit in <i>C.</i> Nam <i>A</i> est in <i>B</i> (ex hyp.). Ergo est aliquod, cui nomen\n[[850.14]] imponemus <i>L</i> tale, ut sit <i>A</i> + <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> (per def. 3 vel charact. 3). Similiter quia <i>B</i> est in <i>C</i> (ex\n[[850.15]] hyp.) erit <i>B</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> in qua assertione pro <i>B</i> ponendo <i>A</i> + <i>L</i> (quae coincidere ostendimus)\n[[850.16]] fiet <i>A</i> + <i>L</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Jam pro <i>L</i> + <i>M</i> ponendo <i>N</i> (per postul. 1) fiet <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Ergo <i>A</i> est\n[[850.17]] in <i>C</i> (per def. 3). Q. E. Dem.\n [[850.18]] <k>Theorema V</k> </p>\n<p> [[850.19]] <b>Cui singula insunt etiam ex ipsis constitutum inest.</b> </p>\n<p> [[850.20]] Si <i>A</i> est in <i>C</i>, et <i>B</i> est in <i>C</i>, etiam <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> (constitutum ex <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>, def. [3]) erit in <i>C.</i>\n[[850.21]] Nam quia <i>A</i> est in <i>C</i> erit aliquod <i>M</i> tale, ut possit fieri <i>A</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> (per def. 3). Similiter\n[[850.22]] quia <i>B</i> est in <i>C</i> poterit fieri <i>B</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Quae conjungendo (per coroll. Theorematis 3) fiet\n[[850.23]] <i>A</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>B</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> + <i>C.</i> Jam <i>C</i> + <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> (per Axiom. 1). Ergo <i>A</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>B</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C.</i> Et\n[[850.24]] proinde (per def. 3) <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> est in <i>C.</i> Q. E. Dem. <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: Intermiscendus familiaris sermo, cui jungendae expressiones propositionum familiares illustrandae exemplis.</Fn>\n [[851.1]] <k>Theorema VI</k> </p>\n<p> [[851.2]] <b>Constitutum ex contentis inest constituto ex continentibus.</b> </p>\n<p> [[851.3]] Si <i>A</i> est in <i>M</i> et <i>B</i> est in <i>N</i> erit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> in <i>M</i> + <i>N.</i> Nam <i>A</i> est in <i>M</i> (ex hyp.) et <i>M</i> est in\n[[851.4]] <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> (per def. 3). Ergo <i>A</i> est in <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> (per theor. 4). Similiter <i>B</i> est in <i>N</i> (ex hyp.) et <i>N</i>\n[[851.5]] est in <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> (per def. 3). Ergo <i>B</i> est in <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> (per th. 4). Jam si <i>A</i> est in <i>M</i> + <i>N</i>, et <i>B</i> est in\n[[851.6]] <i>M</i> + <i>N</i>, etiam (per th. 5) erit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> in <i>M</i> + <i>N.</i> Q. E. Dem.\n [[851.7]] <k>Theorema VII</k> </p>\n<p> [[851.8]] <b>Si quid additur ei cui inest, nil constituitur novi.</b> </p>\n<p> [[851.9]] Seu si <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> erit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A.</i> Nam si <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> potest fieri <i>B</i> + <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> (def. 3).\n[[851.10]] Ergo (per th. 3) <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> + <i>C</i> + <i>B</i>, ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> + <i>C</i> (per axiom. 1), ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> (per dicta hic). Q. E.\n[[851.11]] Dem.\n [[851.12]] <k>Conversum Theorematis praecedentis</k> </p>\n<p> [[851.13]] <b>Si quid addendo alteri nil constituitur novi, ipsum alteri inest.</b> </p>\n<p> [[851.14]] Si <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> tunc <i>B</i> erit in <i>A.</i> Nam <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> (def. 3) et <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> (ex. hyp.).\n[[851.15]] Ergo <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> (per insertum inter th. 2 et 3). Q. E. Dem.\n [[851.16]] <k>Theorema VIII</k> </p>\n<p> [[851.17]] <b>Si coincidentibus detrahantur coincidentia, Residua sunt coincidentia.</b> <Fn><i>Am\n[[851.18]] Rande</i>: Aliud est <b>detractio</b> in notionibus, aliud negatio. V.g. <i>Homo non rationalis</i> est absurdum seu impossibile; sed licet dicere <i>Simia est homo nisi quod non est rationalis</i>; <i>Homines nisi qua bestiis differt homo</i>; ut in Jambo Grotii. <i>Homo ─ Rationalis</i> aliud quam <i>homo non rationalis</i>. Nam <i>homo ─ Rationalis</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Brutum</i>, sed <i>homo non rationalis</i> est impossibile. <i>Homo ─ Animal ─ rational</i> est Nihilum. Hinc detractiones possunt facere nihilum seu non-Ens simplex, imo minus nihilo, sed negationes possunt facere impossibile.</Fn> </p>\n<p> [[851.19]] Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i>, et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i>, erit <i>A ─ B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L ─ M</i>. Nam <i>A ─ B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ B</i> (quod est verum per\n[[851.20]] se) et in alterutro pro <i>A</i> substituendo <i>L</i>, et pro <i>B</i> substituendo <i>M</i> (ex definitione coincidentium)\n[[851.21]] fit <i>A ─ B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L ─ M.</i> Quod Erat Dem.\n [[852.1]] <k>Theorema IX</k> </p>\n<p> [[852.2]] 1) <b>Ex compensatione expressa sequitur destructio compensati, si\n[[852.3]] nihil sit in compensatione destruenda, quod tacite repetitum constitutionem\n[[852.4]] ingrediatur extra compensationem; 2) item si quicquid est\n[[852.5]] hoc repetitum ingrediatur et positionem et detractionem extra compensationem.\n[[852.6]] 3) Si horum neutrum contingat, destructio pro compensatione\n[[852.7]] substitui non potest.</i> </p>\n<p> [[852.8]] <b>Casus 1^#'m^#'u^#'s.</b> Si <i>A</i> + <i>N ─ M ─ N</i> est ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ M</i>, et <i>A, N, M</i> sint incommunicantia. Ita\n[[852.9]] enim nihil est in compensatione destruenda + <i>N</i> ─ <i>N</i>, quod sit extra ipsam in <i>A</i> vel <i>M</i>, seu\n[[852.10]] quod in + <i>N</i> ponitur, id quotiescunque hic ponitur, continetur in + <i>N</i>; et quod in ─<i>N</i>\n[[852.11]] detrahitur, id quotiescunque hic detrahitur, continetur in ─ <i>N</i>, ergo (per ax. 2) pro + <i>N ─ N</i>\n[[852.12]] poni potest, <i>Nihilum</i>. </p>\n<p> [[852.13]] <b>Casus 2.</b> Si <i>A</i> + <i>B ─ B ─ G</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i> et omne quod tam <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>, quam <i>G</i> et <i>B</i> commune\n[[852.14]] habent sit <i>M</i>, erit <i>F</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ G.</i> Ponamus praeterea omne quod <i>A</i> et <i>G</i> commune habent\n[[852.15]] esse <i>E</i>; si quod habent, ita ut si nihil commune habent, <i>E</i> sit ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i>\n [[852.16]] Ita erit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>E</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i>, <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> + <i>M</i> et <i>G</i> ^&.se <Leibniz special character> <i>E</i> + <i>H</i> + <i>M</i>; et fiet\n [[852.17]] <i>F</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>E + Q + M + N + M ─ N ─ M ─ E ─ H─ M</i>, qui termini omnes (<i>E, Q, M, N, H</i>) sunt\n[[852.18]] incommunicantes; ideo (per casum praecedentem) fiet\n [[852.19]] <i>F</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q ─ H</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>E</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M ─ E ─ H ─ M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ G</i>. </p>\n<p> [[852.20]] <b>Casus 3.</b> Si <i>A</i> + <i>B ─ B ─ D</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> et id quod commune est ipsi <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> non coincidit\n[[852.21]] cum eo quod commune est ipsis <i>B</i> et <i>D</i>, non erit <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ D.</i> Sit enim <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>E</i> + <i>F</i> + <i>G</i> et <i>A</i>\n[[852.22]] ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>H</i> + <i>E</i> et <i>D</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>K</i> + <i>F</i>, sic ut haec ingredientia non sint amplius communicantia, nec\n[[853.1]] ulteriore adeo resolutione sit opus, fiet <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>H</i> + <i>E</i> + <i>E</i> + <i>F</i> + <i>G ─ E ─ F ─ G ─ K ─ F</i>, id\n[[853.2]] est (per casum 1) <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>H</i> ─ <i>K</i>, quod non est ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A ─ D</i>, id enim est ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>H</i> + <i>E</i> ─ <i>K</i> ─ <i>F</i>. Nisi\n[[853.3]] ponatur <i>E</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i> seu commune inter <i>B</i> et <i>A</i> idem cum communi inter <i>B</i> et <i>D</i>, contra Hyp.\n[[853.4]] Eadem demonstratio foret, etsi <i>A</i> et <i>D</i> aliquid habuissent commune inter se.\n [[853.5]] <k>Theorema X</k> </p>\n<p> [[853.6]] <b>Detractum et Residuum sunt incommunicantia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[853.7]] Si <i>L ─ A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i>. Dico <i>A</i> et <i>N</i> nihil habere commune. Nam ex definitione detracti et\n[[853.8]] Residui omnia quae sunt in <i>L</i> manent in <i>N</i> praeter ea quae sunt in <i>A</i>, quorum nihil manet\n[[853.9]] in <i>N.</i>\n [[853.10]] <k>Theorema XI</k> </p>\n<p> [[853.11]] <b>In duobus communicantibus id cui inest quicquid utrique commune\n[[853.12]] est, et duo propria sunt tria incommunicantia inter se.</i> </p>\n<p> [[853.13]] Sint <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> communicantia et <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> + <i>M</i>, et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> + <i>M</i>, sic ut quicquid est in <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>,\n[[853.14]] sit in <i>M</i>, nihil vero ejus in <i>P</i> et <i>N</i>, dico <i>P, M, N</i> esse incommunicantia. Nam tam <i>P</i> quam\n[[853.15]] <i>N</i> sunt incommunicantia cum <i>M</i>, quia quod est in <i>M</i> est in <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> simul, at nihil tale est in\n[[853.16]] <i>P</i> aut <i>N.</i> Deinde <i>P</i> et <i>N</i> sunt incommunicantia inter se, alioqui itidem quod ipsis commune\n[[853.17]] est foret in <i>A</i> et <i>B.</i>\n [[853.18]] <k>Problema</k> </p>\n<p> [[853.19]] <b>Efficere ut ex non coincidentibus ad data coincidentia additis constituantur\n[[853.20]] tamen coincidentia.</i> </p>\n<p> [[853.21]] Sit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> dico reperiri posse duo <i>B</i> et <i>N</i>, sic ut <i>B non</i> sit ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> et tamen <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> sit ^&.SE <Leibniz special character>\n[[853.22]] <i>A</i> + <i>N.</i> <b>Solutio.</b> Sumatur aliquid quod insit ipsi <i>A</i> ut <i>M</i>, et sumto <i>N</i> pro arbitrio, sic\n[[853.23]] tamen ut neque <i>M</i> sit in <i>N</i> neque contra <i>N</i> in <i>M</i>, fiat <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i> + <i>N.</i> Et factum erit quod\n[[853.24]] quaeritur. Nam quia <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> ex hyp. et <i>M</i> atque <i>N</i> sibi non insunt ex hyp., et tamen\n[[853.25]] <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>N</i>, quia <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i>, at hoc (per th. 7 quia <i>M</i> est in <i>A</i> ex Hyp.) ^&.SE <Leibniz special character>\n[[853.26]] <i>A</i> + <i>N.</i>\n [[854.1]] <k>Theorema XII</k> </p>\n<p> [[854.2]] <b>In incommunicantibus quae coincidentibus addita faciunt coincidentia,\n[[854.3]] ea ipsa sunt coincidentia.</i> </p>\n<p> [[854.4]] Seu si <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> + <i>D</i> et <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> erit <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>D</i>, modo <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> itemque <i>C</i> et <i>D</i> sint\n[[854.5]] incommunicantia. Nam <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> + <i>D ─ C</i> (per th. 8). Jam <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>A</i>\n[[854.6]] (ex Hyp. quod <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i>) et <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> (per th. 9 cas. 1, quia <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> incommunicantia) et\n[[854.7]] (per eandem rationem) <i>C</i> + <i>D</i> ─ <i>C</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> [<i>D</i>]. Ergo <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> [<i>D</i>]. Quod Erat Dem.\n [[854.8]] <k>Theorema XIII</k> </p>\n<p> [[854.9]] Generaliter <b>Si coincidentibus addendo alia fiant coincidentia, addita\n[[854.10]] sunt inter se communicantia.</i> </p>\n<p> [[854.11]] Sint coincidentia vel eadem <i>A</i> et <i>A</i>, fiatque <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> dico <i>B</i> et <i>N</i> esse\n[[854.12]] communicantia. Nam si <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> sunt incommunicantia, item <i>A</i> et <i>N</i>, erunt <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> (per\n[[854.13]] praeced.). Ergo communicantia sunt <i>B</i> et <i>N.</i> Sin <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> sint communicantia, sit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> +\n[[854.14]] <i>M</i>, et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i>, ponendo <i>M</i> quicquid commune est inter <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> et nihil tale in <i>P</i> et <i>Q.</i>\n[[854.15]] Ergo (per ax. 1) <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N.</i> Jam <i>P, Q, M</i> sunt incommunicantia\n[[854.16]] (per th. 11). Ergo si etiam <i>N</i> cum <i>A</i> seu cum <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> est incommunicans, ex <i>P</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character>\n[[854.17]] <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> fiet (per praeced.) <i>Q</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N.</i> Ergo <i>N</i> est in <i>B.</i> Ergo <i>N</i> et <i>B</i> sunt communicantia. Si\n[[854.18]] vero iisdem positis (nempe <i>P</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> seu <i>A</i> communicante cum <i>B</i>), <i>N</i>\n[[854.19]] etiam communicet cum <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> seu <i>A</i>, tunc <i>N</i> vel communicabit cum <i>M</i>, quo facto\n[[854.20]] communicabit etiam cum <i>B</i> (cui inest <i>M</i>) et habebitur intentum; vel <i>N</i> communicabit cum\n[[854.21]] <i>P</i>, ergo faciamus similiter <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>G</i> + <i>H</i> et <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i> + <i>H</i> sic ut <i>G, H, F</i> sint incommunicantia\n[[854.22]] (secundum th. 11) et ex <i>P</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> fiet <i>G</i> + <i>H</i> + <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>G</i> + <i>H</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>F</i> +\n[[854.23]] <i>H</i>. Ergo (per praeced. th.) fit <i>Q</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F.</i> Ergo <i>N</i> (^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i> + <i>H</i>) et <i>B</i> (^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i>) habent aliquid\n[[854.24]] commune. Q. E. D. </p>\n<p> [[854.25]] <k>Porisma</k> ex demonstratione hac discimus: <b>Si eidem vel coincidentibus\n[[854.26]] addantur aliqua, et fiant coincidentia, sintque addita utraque ei cui\n[[854.27]] adduntur incommunicantia, ipsa coincidere inter se</i> (quod et patet ex\n[[854.28]] th. 12[)]. <b>Sin unum sit communicans eidem illi cui utrumque additur,</b>\n[[855.1]] <b>alterum vero non; tunc incommunicans erit in communicante; denique,\n[[855.2]] si ambo sint communicantia cum eo cui addantur, ad minimum communicabunt\n[[855.3]] inter se (quanquam alioqui non sequatur quae communicant\n[[855.4]] eidem tertio communicare inter se).</i> </p>\n<p> [[855.5]] In Notis: <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>N.</i> Si <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> incommunicantia, item <i>A</i> et <i>N</i> incommunicantia,\n[[855.6]] erit <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i>; si <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> communicantia, at <i>A</i> et <i>N</i> incommunicantia, <i>N</i> erit in <i>B</i>; denique si <i>B</i>\n[[855.7]] communicet cum <i>A</i>, et <i>N</i> itidem communicet cum <i>A</i>, tunc <i>B</i> et <i>N</i> ad minimum communicabunt\n[[855.8]] inter se. </p>\n",
